  "style": {
    "name": "Asravi tide-temple — Mughal grammar in jade",
    "rationale": "Second pass: rebuilt every recess by EXCLUSION (front plane left open, dark_prismarine set deep) so the iwan and eight niches read as true shadow, not painted panels; resolved the four corner minarets into ENGAGED projecting shafts bonded to the wall with continuous gold string-courses tying base/body/drum/minarets into one read; replaced the pyramidal crown with an onion dome whose belly overhangs the drum by two blocks; broke all flat fields with framed two-over-two niche registers, vermilion frets, quartz pilaster dado and rosettes; restored the COLORFUL split-complement hierarchy — jade prismarine dominant, amber gold accent, vermilion punctuation, quartz trim — against the reference's white."
  },
